#
# Counter-example for math:IllFramedPValueShape (Rule I1): the SAME math:PValue as
# conformance-fixtures/pvalue-well-framed.ttl — a math:testStatistic, a
# math:nullHypothesis, and a parameterized math:nullDistribution, with its magnitude a
# framed math:ProbabilityValue — EXCEPT it omits BOTH math:tailDefinition AND
# math:alternativeSidedness. A p-value with a null and a statistic but no tail or
# sidedness is still AMBIGUOUS (one-tailed, two-tailed, and mid-p give different values),
# so the tail-or-sidedness arm of the SHACL-SPARQL frame gate fires —
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (math:IllFramedPValue).
# Single violation: the test, null-hypothesis, test-statistic, and null-distribution arms
# are all satisfied so only the tail/sidedness arm bites; math:AlternativeSidednessValueShape
# (the sh:in gate) is SATISFIED VACUOUSLY because math:alternativeSidedness is absent (no
# value to check); the framed math:ProbabilityValue still satisfies
# math:ProbabilityValueRangeShape, math:ProbabilityValueFramedShape,
# math:ProbabilityScaleDisjointShape and math:RationalValueShape; and the well-formed null
# distribution keeps the P6a/P6b/P7 gates silent — EXACTLY ONE finding.
# Back-reference: math:PValue / math:IllFramedPValue (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecPValueMissingSidednessBad).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:tTestPValue a math:PValue ;
    math:testStatistic ex:tStatistic ;
    math:nullHypothesis ex:noEffectNull ;
    math:nullDistribution ex:tNullDistribution ;
    # NO math:tailDefinition and NO math:alternativeSidedness — the p-value is ambiguous.
    math:pValue ex:pValueMagnitude .

ex:tStatistic a math:Statistic .
ex:noEffectNull a math:NullHypothesis .

ex:tNullDistribution a math:SamplingDistribution ;
    math:distributionFamily ex:normalFamily ;
    math:distributionParameterization ex:meanStddevParameterization ;
    math:hasDistributionParameter ex:meanParam , ex:stddevParam .

ex:normalFamily a math:DistributionFamily .

ex:meanStddevParameterization a math:DistributionParameterization ;
    math:requiresParameterRole ex:meanRole , ex:stddevRole .

ex:meanRole a math:DistributionParameterRole .
ex:stddevRole a math:DistributionParameterRole .

ex:meanParam a math:DistributionParameter ;
    math:parameterRole ex:meanRole .

ex:stddevParam a math:DistributionParameter ;
    math:parameterRole ex:stddevRole .

ex:pValueMagnitude a math:ProbabilityValue , math:RationalValue ;
    math:numerator 3 ;         # 3/100 = 0.03, within [0, 1]
    math:denominator 100 ;
    gmeow:hasReferenceFrame ex:samplingFrame .

ex:samplingFrame a gmeow:ReferenceFrame .
<http://example.org/math/pValueMagnitude> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/hasDimension> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/dimensionless> .
